ละตำ, 52\nการยืนขอม, 73\nข้อมูลบวก, XXXIX\nข้อมูล, เป็นคครับ, 35\nข้อมูลบวกบางบาง, 29\nข้อความบวกเป็นคครับบวก, 15\nคคความ, 29\nข้อมูล, XXIX\nพิการบวก, XXIX\nมูลบวกและตำ, ใน, 59\nข้อมูลคครับบวก, 73\nข้อมูลบวกบวกระบวน, 42\nข้อมูลบวกบวกบวก, 11\nข้อมูลบวกบวกในบวกบวกและตำ, 67\nข้อมูลบวกบวกบวกที่ใช้คำ, 71\nข้อมูลบวก, 29\nข้อมูลบวกระบวน, 44\nข้อมูลบวก, 13\nข้อมูลบวกในบวกบวกและตำ, 69\nระบุบอน, 73\nข้อมูลบวกบวกบวก, 98\nข้อมูลบอน, ใน, 80\nข้อมูลบอน, มิคค, 89\nข้อมูลบอน, ใน, 80\nข้อมูลบอน, มิคค, 89\nข้อมูลบวกบวกบวก, 46\nGet it on Google play\nกลุ่มวิธีบทที่ต้องการแสดงในหนึ่ง\nDEPARTMENT OF MEDICAL SCIENCES"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/thp/appendices/appendix-1-general-information","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"APPENDIX 1 GENERAL INFORMATION"},"edition":"THP-2021-Supplement-2025","category":"appendices","definition":{"en":"The specifications given below are strictly for the use of the materials as reagents. The inclusion of a material in this Appendix does not imply that it is suitable for use in medicines. Exceptionally, a trademark or supplier may be indicated for certain reagents whose availability is limited. It is however acceptable to use reagents from another source provided that they comply with the standards of the Pharmacopoeia.\n\n## 1.1 REAGENTS\n\nThe name of a substance or solution indicates a reagent included in the following list. The specifications given for reagents do not necessarily guarantee their quality for use in medicines.\n\nSome of the reagents included may be injurious to health. Important cautions have been stated for these reagents. They should be handled in accordance with good laboratory practice and any relevant regulations.\n\nReagents in aqueous solution are prepared using water. Where the name of the solvent is not stated, an aqueous solution is intended.\n\nUnless otherwise specified, the reagents and reagent solutions are to be stored in well containers. The labelling should comply with the relevant national legislation.\n\n## Alanine $ \\mathrm{C_{3} H_{7} N O_{2}}=8 9. 0 9 $\n\nUse an analytical reagent grade of commerce containing not less than 98.0 per cent w/w of $ \\mathrm{C_{3} H_{7} N O_{2}}. $\n\nDESCRIPTION White, crystalline powder; odourless.\n\nSOLUBILITY Freely soluble in water; slightly soluble in ethanol.\n\nMELTING TEMPERATURE About $ 2 9 7^{\\circ} $ , with decomposition (Appendix 4.3).\n\nStore in tightly closed containers.\n\n## Aluminium Chloride, Anhydrous $ \\mathrm{A l C l_{3}}=1 3 3. 3 4 $\n\nDESCRIPTION White, crystalline powder; odour, strong of hydrogen chloride.\n\nSOLUBILITY Freely soluble in many organic solvents such as benzophenone, nitrobenzene;\n\nsoluble in benzene, in carbon tetrachloride, and in chloroform.\n\nMELTING TEMPERATURE About $ 1 9 3^{\\circ} $ (Appendix 4.3).\n\nStore in tightly closed containers, protected from moisture.\n\nBetulinic Acid $ \\mathrm{C_{30}H_{48}O_{3}}=4 5 6. 70 $\n\nDESCRIPTION White, crystalline powder.\n\nMELTING RANGE $ 3 1 6^{\\circ} $ to $ 3 1 8^{\\circ} $ (Appendix 4.3).\n\nStore in tightly closed containers.\n\nBlumeatin $ \\mathrm{C_{16}H_{14}O_{6}}=302.28 $\n\nUse an analytical reagent grade of commerce containing not less than 95.0 per cent w/w of $ \\mathrm{C_{17}H_{14}O_{6}}. $\n\nDESCRIPTION Yellow, crystalline powder.\n\nSOLUBILITY Soluble in dimethyl sulfoxide.\n\nStore in tightly closed containers.\n\n## Hesperidin $ \\mathrm{C_{28}H_{34}O_{15}}=610.56 $\n\nDESCRIPTION Light brown, crystalline powder. MELTING RANGE $ 2 5 0^{\\circ} $ to $ 2 5 5^{\\circ} $ (Appendix 4.3). Store in tightly closed containers.\n\n## Luteolin $ \\mathrm{C_{1 5} H_{1 0}O_{6}}=2 8 6. 2 4 $\n\nUse an analytical reagent grade of commerce containing not less than 98.0 per cent w/w of $ \\mathrm{C_{1 5} H_{1 0} O_{6}}. $\n\nDESCRIPTION Yellow, crystalline powder.\n\n$$\n3 3 0 ^ {\\circ}\n$$\n\nStore in tightly closed containers at a temperature between $ 2^{\\circ} $ and $ 8^{\\circ} $ , protected from light.\n\n## $ \\alpha $ - Mangostin $ \\mathrm{C_{24}H_{26}O_{6}}=410.46 $\n\nUse an analytical reagent grade of commerce containing not less than 98.0 per cent w/w of $ \\mathrm{C_{24}H_{26}O_{6}} $.\n\nDESCRIPTION Yellow, crystalline solid.\n\nSOLUBILITY Soluble in methanol.\n\nMELTING TEMPERATURE About $ 182^{\\circ} $ (Appendix 4.3).\n\nStore in tightly closed containers at a temperature between $ 4^{\\circ} $ and $ 8^{\\circ} $.\n\n## Naringin $ \\mathrm{C_{2 7} H_{3 2} O_{1 4}}=5 8 0. 5 3 $\n\nUse an analytical reagent grade of commerce containing not less than 95.0 per cent w/w of $ \\mathrm{C_{27}H_{32}O_{14}} $.\n\nDESCRIPTION Light brown, crystalline powder.\n\nSOLUBILITY Slightly soluble in water.\n\nMELTING TEMPERATURE About $ 83^{\\circ} $ (Appendix 4.3).\n\nStore in tightly closed containers.\n\n## Terpinen-4-ol $ \\mathrm{C_{1 0} H_{1 8} O}=1 5 4. 2 5 $\n\nUse an analytical reagent grade of commerce containing not less than 95.0 per cent w/w of $ \\mathrm{C_{10}H"},"sections":[{"name":"Preamble","text":"The specifications given below are strictly for the use of the materials as reagents. The inclusion of a material in this Appendix does not imply that it is suitable for use in medicines. Exceptionally, a trademark or supplier may be indicated for certain reagents whose availability is limited. It is however acceptable to use reagents from another source provided that they comply with the standards of the Pharmacopoeia.\n1.1 REAGENTS\nThe name of a substance or solution indicates a reagent included in the following list. The specifications given for reagents do not necessarily guarantee their quality for use in medicines.\nSome of the reagents included may be injurious to health. Important cautions have been stated for these reagents. They should be handled in accordance with good laboratory practice and any relevant regulations.\nReagents in aqueous solution are prepared using water. Where the name of the solvent is not stated, an aqueous solution is intended.\nUnless otherwise specified, the reagents and reagent solutions are to be stored in well containers. The labelling should comply with the relevant national legislation.\nAlanine \\mathrm{C_{3} H_{7} N O_{2}}=8 9. 0 9\nUse an analytical reagent grade of commerce containing not less than 98.0 per cent w/w of \\mathrm{C_{3} H_{7} N O_{2}}."},{"name":"Description","text":"White, crystalline powder; odourless."},{"name":"Solubility","text":"Freely soluble in water; slightly soluble in ethanol.\nMELTING TEMPERATURE About 2 9 7° , with decomposition (Appendix 4.3).\nStore in tightly closed containers.\nAluminium Chloride, Anhydrous \\mathrm{A l C l_{3}}=1 3 3. 3 4"},{"name":"Description","text":"White, crystalline powder; odour, strong of hydrogen chloride."},{"name":"Solubility","text":"Freely soluble in many organic solvents such as benzophenone, nitrobenzene;\nsoluble in benzene, in carbon tetrachloride, and in chloroform.\nMELTING TEMPERATURE About 1 9 3° (Appendix 4.3).\nStore in tightly closed containers, protected from moisture.\nBetulinic Acid \\mathrm{C_{30}H_{48}O_{3}}=4 5 6. 70"},{"name":"Description","text":"White, crystalline powder.\nMELTING RANGE 3 1 6° to 3 1 8° (Appendix 4.3).\nStore in tightly closed containers.\nBlumeatin \\mathrm{C_{16}H_{14}O_{6}}=302.28\nUse an analytical reagent grade of commerce containing not less than 95.0 per cent w/w of \\mathrm{C_{17}H_{14}O_{6}}.\nYellow, crystalline powder."},{"name":"Solubility","text":"Soluble in dimethyl sulfoxide.\nStore in tightly closed containers.\nHesperidin \\mathrm{C_{28}H_{34}O_{15}}=610.56"},{"name":"Description","text":"Light brown, crystalline powder. MELTING RANGE 2 5 0° to 2 5 5° (Appendix 4.3). Store in tightly closed containers.\nLuteolin \\mathrm{C_{1 5} H_{1 0}O_{6}}=2 8 6. 2 4\nUse an analytical reagent grade of commerce containing not less than 98.0 per cent w/w of \\mathrm{C_{1 5} H_{1 0} O_{6}}.\nYellow, crystalline powder.\n$3 3 0 ^ {\\circ}Store in tightly closed containers at a temperature between 2° and 8° , protected from light.\nα - Mangostin \\mathrm{C_{24}H_{26}O_{6}}=410.46 Use an analytical reagent grade of commerce containing not less than 98.0 per cent w/w of \\mathrm{C_{24}H_{26}O_{6}} .\nYellow, crystalline solid."},{"name":"Solubility","text":"Soluble in methanol.\nMELTING TEMPERATURE About 182° (Appendix 4.3).\nStore in tightly closed containers at a temperature between 4° and 8° .\nNaringin \\mathrm{C_{2 7} H_{3 2} O_{1 4}}=5 8 0. 5 3 Use an analytical reagent grade of commerce containing not less than 95.0 per cent w/w of \\mathrm{C_{27}H_{32}O_{14}} ."},{"name":"Description","text":"Light brown, crystalline powder."},{"name":"Solubility","text":"Slightly soluble in water.\nMELTING TEMPERATURE About 83° (Appendix 4.3).\nStore in tightly closed containers.\nTerpinen-4-ol \\mathrm{C_{1 0} H_{1 8} O}=1 5 4. 2 5 Use an analytical reagent grade of commerce containing not less than 95.0 per cent w/w of \\mathrm{C_{10}H_{18}O} DESCRIPTION Colourless to pale yellow, oily liquid. SOLUBILITY Soluble in oils; slightly soluble in water. BOILING TEMPERATURE About 209° (Appendix 4.6). Store in tightly closed containers, protected from light, and at a temperature between 2° and 8° ## INDEX\nA\nAdditional Information, 6\nAlanine,173\nAluminium Chloride, Anhydrous,173\nAmendments, XXIX\nArsenic and Heavy Metals,5\nAsian Mint,108\nAurantium maximum Burm.,134\nAuthenticated Reference Specimens,3\nB\nBak Nao, Phio, 83\nBakkham, Nuea Nai Malet, 77\nBiancaea sappan (L.) Tod., 23\nBiancaeae Sappan Lignum, 23\nBetulinic acid, 173\nBlumea balsamifera (L.) DC, 100\nBlumea Balsamifera Leaf, 100\nBlumeae Balsamiferae Folium, 100\nBlumeatin, 173\nBridelia ovata Decne., 69\nBridelia ovata Decne. var. genuina Müll. Arg., 69\nBridelia Ovata Leaf, 69\nBrideliae Ovatae Folium, 69\nC\nCaesalpinia sappan L., 23\nCalysaccion siamense Miq., 122"},{"name":"Category","text":"and Dose, 6\nCeylon Leadwort Root, 11\nChettamun Phloeng Daeng, Rak, 17\nChettamun Phloeng Khao, Ra